>
> You can't get more gold out of a shopkeeper than the amount he has.

But you can get arbitrary amounts of credit. Say you're making a huge amount
of credit in one shop where you have some really expensive items to steal
and resell, then you clone that credit into gold until the shopkeeper is
broke and you've taken all of his interesting stuff. Now the remaining
credit goes to waste. But with an actual credit card, you could use that
credit to clone more gold out of another shopkeeper.

This makes an existing strategy a little more "abusable", even if not by
much. But how else is it going to be used? IMO the only time when you have
considerable amounts of credit in a shop and nothing to spend it on is when
you created that credit by stealing. So if you said that credit cloning was
to be made harder, this YANI wouldn't make sense.


